  "raw": {
    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49865": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Accounting",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty - Accounting Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty - Accounting Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution Northern State University Working Title Adjunct Faculty - Accounting Posting Number F01951P Department NSU-Accounting Physical Location of Position (City) Posting Text Northern State University’s School of Business invites applications for part-time adjunct accounting instructors to meet current and future teaching needs. We are seeking qualified candidates for both online and in-person instruction, with assignments based on departmental needs, instructor qualifications, and course availability. Potential teaching assignments include: Principles of Accounting I ( ACCT 210) Principles of Accounting II ( ACCT 211) Intermediate Accounting I ( ACCT 310) Intermediate Accounting II ( ACCT 311) Accounting Systems ( ACCT 360) Income Tax Accounting ( ACCT 430) Teaching assignments will be made on current and future departmental needs. Applicants are encouraged to identify the accounting courses and instructional formats for which they are qualified and interested in teaching. Required Education and Experience: • Master’s degree in accounting, or a master’s degree in business administration or related field with an emphasis, concentration, or substantial graduate coursework in accounting from an accredited institution of higher learning • Academic preparation and/or professional experience in accounting appropriate to the course(s) to be taught. Candidates with substantial professional accounting experience are encouraged to apply, including those whose graduate degree is in a related business discipline. Preferred Qualifications: • Previous teaching experience in higher education, including experience teaching online, adult, or non-traditional learners • Relevant professional certifications, such as CPA , CIA , CISA , or CFE • Current professional experience or demonstrated expertise in one or more of the accounting areas from the courses listed above Posting Date 09/24/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 10/15/2026 Advertised Salary Duration of the Term Other If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Tenure Status Term Proposed Rank Assistant Professor Work Hours Varies Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Temporary Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search Department Description and Cultural Expectations Northern State University is a premier residential institution characterized by outstanding instruction, extraordinary community relations, and unparalleled extracurricular opportunities. NSU has been named one of the Midwest’s best undergraduate institutions by US News and World Report for many years. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission, and the School of Business is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs ( ACBSP ). The School of Business is housed in the state-of-the-art Business and Health Innovation Center. Northern is located in Aberdeen, South Dakota, a vibrant community of approximately 28,000 residents that serves as a retail and service hub for northeastern South Dakota and the surrounding region. The university enjoys a strong relationship with the Aberdeen community and the broader region. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Northern State University is committed to building a welcoming culture of belonging and collegiality that respects diversity in knowledge, culture and world view. Northern seeks faculty and staff who will engage with individuals of diverse backgrounds, beliefs and perspectives to increase awareness, understanding, respect and opportunity for all. Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position. Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Analyzing, Comprehend, Frequent Change, Intense Customer Interaction, Logic, Memory, Multiple Priorities, Multiple Stimuli, Pace-average, Perform calculations, Reading, Reasoning, Verbal Communication, Written Communication Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. If other protection is used please identify Physical Requirements Please designate the physical requirements of this position Lifting light, Sitting for sustained periods of time, Standing for sustained periods of time, Use Both Hands, Use of Either Hand, Independently, Walking, Wrist Movement (twisting or rotating) Describe any of the conditions selected Sensory Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the sensory requirements for this position. Hearing, Speaking, Vision (With and without corrective lenses) Working Conditions & Exposures Working Conditions or Exposures (or potential exposures) that this position may encounter during the course of the work day. Please describe, in more detail, any of the conditions checked above Working Environment Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Classroom Environment If you have indicated Other Environment, if work tasks involve one or more of the above, or if further explanation is necessary, please use the space provided. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Optional Documents The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
